---
// Two ways to read a type 2 dimension from one fact row: the version it points at ("as it was") and that customer's current row ("as it is").
---
<figure class="awi">
  <div class="awi-fact">fact row: order 2646 on 2024-12-10, <code>customer_key = 8</code></div>
  <div class="awi-grid">
    <div class="awi-path">
      <h4>As it was</h4>
      <p>join on <code>customer_key</code></p>
      <div class="awi-row">key 8 · customer 8 · <b>Bronze</b><span>1900-01-01 to 2025-07-01</span></div>
      <p class="awi-note">the tier on the day of the sale</p>
    </div>
    <div class="awi-path">
      <h4>As it is</h4>
      <p>key → <code>customer_id</code> → row with <code>is_current = 1</code></p>
      <div class="awi-row awi-cur">key 9 · customer 8 · <b>Silver</b><span>2025-07-01 to 9999-12-31</span></div>
      <p class="awi-note">the tier today, applied to every sale</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>The fact stores one key, which always means "as it was". To ask "as it is", step from that version to the customer's durable id, then to the current version. A third question, "as of a date", picks the version valid on a date you choose.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style is:inline>
.awi { margin: 20px 0; }
.awi-fact { border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 6px 10px; text-align: center; font-size: 14px; background: var(--surface); }
.awi-grid { display: grid; gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); }
.awi-path { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--surface); }
.awi h4 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 15px; }
.awi-path p { margin: 4px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
.awi-row { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 8px; font-size: 13.5px; }
.awi-row span { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
.awi-cur { background: var(--accent-soft); }
.awi-note { font-style: italic; }
.awi figcaption { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
